,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,1372,220,17,19,646,387,1865,553,84192,3786,3040,10250,5109,25,220,17,11,220,17,11,220,17,323,220,18,13,2585,1657,49433,1969,387,54916,311,1281,220,17,19,15,15,1939,37314,9960,510,27,37420,91339,397,1249,8253,1246,1657,10250,5109,1969,387,54916,311,1281,220,17,19,15,15,11,582,1191,553,9271,279,10250,8168,2022,315,220,17,19,15,15,382,16,13,3070,32306,37729,2022,315,220,17,19,15,15,25,1019,256,481,5512,11,582,21749,220,17,19,15,15,553,279,24632,10250,1372,11,892,374,220,17,624,257,1124,9640,257,220,17,19,15,15,1124,611,220,17,284,220,16,17,15,15,198,257,1124,921,256,481,1205,3060,49702,553,220,17,510,257,1124,9640,257,220,16,17,15,15,1124,611,220,17,284,220,21,15,15,198,257,1124,921,257,1124,9640,257,220,21,15,15,1124,611,220,17,284,220,18,15,15,198,257,1124,921,257,1124,9640,257,220,18,15,15,1124,611,220,17,284,220,16,20,15,198,257,1124,921,257,1124,9640,257,220,16,20,15,1124,611,220,17,284,220,22,20,198,257,1124,921,256,481,4695,11,220,22,20,374,537,74916,553,220,17,11,773,582,3271,311,279,1790,24632,10250,1372,11,892,374,220,18,624,257,1124,9640,257,220,22,20,1124,611,220,18,284,220,17,20,198,257,1124,921,256,481,9295,11,220,17,20,374,537,74916,553,220,18,11,773,582,3271,311,279,1790,24632,10250,1372,11,892,374,220,20,624,257,1124,9640,257,220,17,20,1124,611,220,20,284,220,20,198,257,1124,921,257,1124,9640,257,220,20,1124,611,220,20,284,220,16,198,257,1124,21675,522,37420,91339,29,151645,198,151644,872,198,2610,1231,312,18883,55856,279,3491,323,18130,279,6291,504,279,7167,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe number 24 can be made by multiplying together four prime numbers: 2, 2, 2 and 3. How many primes must be multiplied to make 2400?\n\nPartial draft:\n<partial_draft>\nTo determine how many prime numbers must be multiplied to make 2400, we start by finding the prime factorization of 2400.\n\n1. **Prime Factorization of 2400:**\n   - First, we divide 2400 by the smallest prime number, which is 2.\n     \\[\n     2400 \\div 2 = 1200\n     \\]\n   - We continue dividing by 2:\n     \\[\n     1200 \\div 2 = 600\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     600 \\div 2 = 300\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     300 \\div 2 = 150\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     150 \\div 2 = 75\n     \\]\n   - Now, 75 is not divisible by 2, so we move to the next smallest prime number, which is 3.\n     \\[\n     75 \\div 3 = 25\n     \\]\n   - Next, 25 is not divisible by 3, so we move to the next smallest prime number, which is 5.\n     \\[\n     25 \\div 5 = 5\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     5 \\div 5 = 1\n     \\]\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"You may re-analyze the problem and rewrite the solution from the beginning.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"e046df3b5379e0f0d7e2e56ea62fdf43e2d3cc0803f00e260b4e3809bd9f840b"},"seconds":29.923274755477905,"seed":1022485419845042843,"stop":"eos","text":"To determine how many prime numbers must be multiplied to make 2400, we start by finding the prime factorization of 2400.\n\n1. **Prime Factorization of 2400:**\n   - We divide 2400 by the smallest prime number, which is 2.\n     \\[\n     2400 \\div 2 = 1200\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     1200 \\div 2 = 600\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     600 \\div 2 = 300\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     300 \\div 2 = 150\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     150 \\div 2 = 75\n     \\]\n   - Now, 75 is not divisible by 2, so we move to the next smallest prime number, which is 3.\n     \\[\n     75 \\div 3 = 25\n     \\]\n   - Next, 25 is not divisible by 3, so we move to the next smallest prime number, which is 5.\n     \\[\n     25 \\div 5 = 5\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     5 \\div 5 = 1\n     \\]\n\nFrom the steps above, we can write the prime factorization of 2400 as:\n\\[\n2400 = 2^5 \\times 3^1 \\times 5^2\n\\]\n\n2. **Counting the Prime Factors:**\n   - The prime factorization includes the prime numbers 2, 3, and 5.\n   - The exponent of 2 is 5, so there are 5 factors of 2.\n   - The exponent of 3 is 1, so there is 1 factor of 3.\n   - The exponent of 5 is 2, so there are 2 factors of 5.\n\nAdding these together, we have:\n\\[\n5 + 1 + 2 = 8\n\\]\n\nThus, the total number of prime factors needed to make 2400 is \\(\\boxed{8}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{8}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To determine how many prime numbers must be multiplied to make 2400, we start by finding the prime factorization of 2400.\n\n1. **Prime Factorization of 2400:**\n   - We divide 2400 by the smallest prime number, which is 2.\n     \\[\n     2400 \\div 2 = 1200\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     1200 \\div 2 = 600\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     600 \\div 2 = 300\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     300 \\div 2 = 150\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     150 \\div 2 = 75\n     \\]\n   - Now, 75 is not divisible by 2, so we move to the next smallest prime number, which is 3.\n     \\[\n     75 \\div 3 = 25\n     \\]\n   - Next, 25 is not divisible by 3, so we move to the next smallest prime number, which is 5.\n     \\[\n     25 \\div 5 = 5\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     5 \\div 5 = 1\n     \\]\n\nFrom the steps above, we can write the prime factorization of 2400 as:\n\\[\n2400 = 2^5 \\times 3^1 \\times 5^2\n\\]\n\n2. **Counting the Prime Factors:**\n   - The prime factorization includes the prime numbers 2, 3, and 5.\n   - The exponent of 2 is 5, so there are 5 factors of 2.\n   - The exponent of 3 is 1, so there is 1 factor of 3.\n   - The exponent of 5 is 2, so there are 2 factors of 5.\n\nAdding these together, we have:\n\\[\n5 + 1 + 2 = 8\n\\]\n\nThus, the total number of prime factors needed to make 2400 is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).","id":"prealgebra:753"}
